<title>UK: Arcadian buys UK hotel for 4.4 mln stg.</title>
<headline>Arcadian buys UK hotel for 4.4 mln stg.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>UK hotels operator Arcadian International Plc said on Thursday it had bought Chilston Park Ltd, which owns Chilston Park Hotel, for 4.4 million stg.</p>
<p>It said in a statement that the hotel, situated in Kent, south east England, was expected to have net operating profit of 479,000 stg for 1996.</p>
<p>Arcadian also said that it had granted Homewood Park Ltd an option to acquire its hotel Hunstrete House, situated in Bath, south west England, for 1.86 million stg.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
